EXP1 :-
👇

🔹 Core Idea

Your program implements a dictionary using a Binary Search Tree (BST).

Each node stores a word + meaning
Words are arranged alphabetically:
Smaller → left
Larger → right
🔹 Main Operations
Insert (addNode)
Places word in correct position using BST rules.
Display
Ascending → Left → Root → Right (sorted order)
Descending → Right → Root → Left
Search
Compares word and moves left/right → counts comparisons.
Update
Searches word, then updates its meaning.
Height (height)
Finds longest path → shows max comparisons (worst case).
Delete Tree
Deletes all nodes using postorder traversal.
🔹 Key Concept
Faster than linear search


EXP2:-
👇
🔹 Core Idea

This program builds an Expression Tree from a Prefix expression (like +--a*bc/def).

Operands → leaf nodes (a, b, c…)
Operators → internal nodes (+, -, *, /)
🔹 How Tree is Constructed (constructTree)
Traverse prefix from right to left
If operand → push to stack
If operator →
pop 2 nodes
make them left & right children
push new node back

👉 Stack helps build the tree correctly.

🔹 Traversals
Inorder (inorder)
→ Left → Root → Right
→ Gives infix form (without brackets)
Print Expression (printTree)
→ Adds brackets to show correct expression
👉 Example: (a-(b*c))
Postorder (postorder)
→ Left → Right → Root
→ Uses 2 stacks (non-recursive)
🔹 Delete Tree
Recursively deletes all nodes (postorder)
Prevents memory leaks
🔹 Key Concept
Expression tree represents mathematical expressions
Traversals give:
Inorder → infix
Postorder → postfix


